# Cloudflare Pages redirect map. Replaces the 301 block in the old
# public/.htaccess, which Pages does not read.
#
# Format: /source  /destination  status. Rules are evaluated top to bottom and
# the first match wins, so the nested WordPress service URLs are listed before
# the top-level ones. Every source below has a matching /source/ line right
# after it: Cloudflare Pages matches _redirects against the raw request path
# before any trailing-slash normalization, and the old WordPress URLs were all
# published *with* a trailing slash — a slash-less rule alone would miss every
# real inbound link and search result.
#
# Three things the old .htaccess did are handled natively by Pages and need no
# rule here: trailing-slash removal, directory indexes
# (/services/veneers -> /services/veneers/index.html), and the custom 404,
# which Pages serves from dist/404.html automatically.
#
# Do NOT blanket-redirect /wp-content/* — third parties hotlink those assets
# and redirecting them manufactures soft 404s. Let them 404.

